#E = 6
  curve: y^2 = x^3 + 1 over F_5
  trace: t = p + 1 - #E = 0
  how: Schoof: t mod l from the Frobenius on E[l] (division polynomials), CRT
  residues: t = 0 mod 2, 0 mod 3, 0 mod 7
  per prime: l = 3: degree 4; l = 7: degree 24
  check: Hasse: |t| <= 2 sqrt(p)
  check: (2, 2) has order 6 (N P = O, and (N/q) P != O stepwise for each prime q of N)
  check: N = 6 is the only multiple of 6 in the Hasse interval [2, 10]
